 is designed to support the Navy\'s future surface combatant requirements. Companies selected for testing include General Dynamics, Lockheed Martin, and Northrop Grumman. The testing will take place at sea to evaluate the vessel\'s performance in various scenarios, including anti-submarine warfare and surface combat.\n\nID: 4156476\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: us-navy-selects-hii-usv-advance-atsea-539881\nTEXT: The US Navy has selected HII\'s ROMULUS unmanned surface vessel to advance to the at-sea testing phase of the Medium Unmanned Surface Vessel (MUSV) program. Andy Green, executive vice president of HII and president of its Mission Technologies division, said this milestone reflects HII\'s track record for delivering mission-ready autonomous capabilities. The ROMULUS USV is designed to meet the Navy\'s requirements, delivering high-endurance autonomy for intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance, as well as counter-unmanned air systems and mine countermeasures.\n\n\n',)
