2026-06-05 02:35:45 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\nYou are given a list of RawRecord objects. Each RawRecord contains:\n- raw_id\n- text\n- metadata (including a \'created\' field representing when the record was published)\n\nYour task is to infer the single canonical semantic triple that best represents\nthe shared meaning across ALL records in the list.\n\nA triple has the form:\n(subject, predicate, object)\n\nRules:\n1. The triple must express the core relation that all records instantiate.\n2. The triple must be abstract enough to cover all records, but specific enough\n   to distinguish this subgraph from unrelated content.\n3. Use canonicalized forms of entities and relations.\n4. The predicate should be a relation phrase, not a full sentence.\n5. Ignore surface details and stylistic differences.\n6. Do NOT summarize the documents. Extract the underlying relation.\n7. If multiple triples are possible, choose the one that is maximally general\n   while still being true for all records.\n\nYou must also infer contextual metadata with the following keys:\n- location\n- subject_matter\n- industry\n- time  ← IMPORTANT: this should reflect WHEN THE EVENT OCCURRED,\n         not when the records were published.\n\nYou may use the \'created\' timestamps to help disambiguate event time,\nbut you must NOT output the \'created\' timestamps themselves.\n\nOnly include a metadata field if it is stable across ALL records.\nIf a field is not stable, set it to null.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4155814\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: article-e176533b-d0c7-5db0-920b-2550f04f2d4f-html\nTEXT: Indonesian authorities have searched the office of a free meals agency after its leader, Prabowo, was fired. The search, led by investigators from the Attorney General\'s Office, aimed to investigate issues related to discipline in following standard operating procedures and implementing governance. The agency\'s new leader, Nanik S. Deyang, was previously the deputy chief. The search did not disclose what specific case was being investigated. The free meals program, which aims to combat malnutrition and support farmers by purchasing their harvests, is expected to cost $28 billion through 2029.\n\nID: 4155692\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: kpai-urges-bgn-to-prioritize-vulnerable-regions-in-free-meals-program\nTEXT: Indonesia\'s Child Protection Agency (KPAI) urged the National Nutrition Agency (BGN) to prioritize food-insecure regions in implementing the Free Nutritious Meals program. KPAI Deputy Chair Jasra Putra emphasized the need for phased implementation in areas facing severe food insecurity, malnutrition, and socio-economic vulnerability. The agency also recommended alternative delivery models, such as using school cafeterias to reduce contamination risks, and stricter standards for nutritional quality and food safety. Putra emphasized the importance of public participation in supporting and monitoring implementation, as well as ensuring the program remains free from intimidation or practices that could threaten children\'s physical or psychological safety.\n\nID: 4155673\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: ministry-digitalizes-milk-collection-points-to-strengthen-supply-chain\nTEXT: The Indonesian Ministry has digitalized 96 milk collection points in West Java and East Java, involving over 12,000 dairy farmers. This move aims to strengthen the domestic dairy industry by improving raw material quality and product innovation, with a goal of increasing public milk consumption. The digitalization program is part of the ministry\'s efforts to address Indonesia\'s lower milk consumption per capita, currently at around 17.76 liters annually, compared to Malaysia, Singapore, and Vietnam.\n\nID: 4155667\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: bgn-leadership-shakeup-aimed-at-boosting-free-meal-program\nTEXT: State Secretary Minister Prasetyo Hadi emphasized that the leadership change at the National Nutrition Agency (BGN) will not disrupt Indonesia\'s Free Nutritious Meals program, but rather strengthen its services. President Prabowo Subianto decided to replace BGN head Dadan Hindayana, along with deputy heads Lodewyk Pusung and Sony Sanjaya, after nearly 1.5 years of monitoring their performance. The BGN plays a strategic role in supporting the government\'s agenda to improve public nutrition, requiring robust governance and effective cross-sector coordination. The new leadership will focus on internal consolidation, strengthening coordination across ministries and agencies, and enhancing collaboration with regional governments. The Free Nutritious Meals program targets 82.9 million beneficiaries nationwide, aiming to improve the nutritional status of children under five and other vulnerable groups.\n\nID: 4155662\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: indonesia-launches-milk-kitchen-to-boost-dairy-supply-for-mbg\nTEXT: The Indonesian government is launching the "Indonesian Milk Kitchen" (Dasi) concept to boost dairy supply for the Free Nutritional Meals (MBG) program. The Ministry of Agriculture aims to support small-scale milk processing units integrated with MBG kitchens across regions, connecting farmers\' fresh milk production to the program. Director of Livestock Product Downstreaming Makmun stated that Dasi is designed to expand dairy cattle development in regions such as Sumatra, Kalimantan, and Sulawesi. The program seeks to create a stable market for farmers and encourage local milk processing units, with the goal of increasing dairy cattle productivity above 20 liters per day.\n\nID: 4155598\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: bem-ui-urges-total-review-of-mbg-after-dadans-dismissal\nTEXT: The Executive Board of the University of Indonesia\'s Student Body (BEM UI) is urging a thorough review of the Free Nutritious Meal (MBG) program following Dadan Hindayana\'s dismissal as Head of the National Nutrition Agency. BEM UI Chairperson Yatalathof Ma\'shum Imawan believes the change in leadership is a signal that the government acknowledges serious issues with MBG\'s implementation. He states that the removal of Hindayana is an indirect acknowledgment of problems with supervision, budget utilization, and on-the-ground implementation. BEM UI demands a total evaluation of the MBG program, including cessation of its implementation and redirecting funds to more urgent needs. They also request disclosure of MBG data, including problematic SPPGs and parties involved in program implementation.\n\nID: 4155596\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: ago-raids-bgn-office-hours-after-prabowo-reshuffles-agency-leadership\nTEXT: Indonesia\'s Attorney General\'s Office raided the office of BGN, a national nutrition agency, following Prabowo Subianto\'s reshuffling of the agency leadership. Director Syarief Sulaiman Nahdi and acting head Muhammad Jefri of the Legal Information Center have not confirmed the raid. The move comes a week after rumors surfaced that AGO conducted a sting operation against BGN officials, which the agency denied.\n\nID: 4155594\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: prabowos-bgn-reshuffle-will-not-disrupt-free-meal-program-palace-says\nTEXT: Indonesia\'s Palace says Prabowo\'s BGN reshuffle won\'t disrupt free meal program. \n\nPrasetyo stated that the government aims to improve organizational governance and provide real benefits to the community, particularly in improving nutrition quality. \n\nNot News Article\n\nID: 4155593\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: dadan-hindayanas-controversies-during-his-time-as-bgn-chief\nTEXT: Dadan Hindayanas, the former Head of the National Nutrition Agency (BGN), has been dismissed from his position after serving for approximately one and a half years. The decision was made by the President following a performance review, which highlighted various controversies during Dadan\'s tenure. These include his statement that drinking two liters of milk per day is beneficial for growth, as well as proposing insects and sago worms as alternative protein sources in the Free Nutritious Meal (MBG) program. Additionally, under Dadan\'s leadership, the MBG program has been linked to 446 poisoning cases with a total of 37,693 victims as of early May 2026. The procurement practices at BGN have also been criticized for being wasteful and suspicious, with examples including the purchase of 20,000 motorcycle units and shoe polish.\n\n\n',)
2026-06-05 02:35:45 [DEBUG] llm.engine: KWARGS: {}
