stated that the government aims to improve organizational governance and provide real benefits to the community, particularly in improving nutrition quality. \n\nNot News Article\n\nID: 4155593\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: dadan-hindayanas-controversies-during-his-time-as-bgn-chief\nTEXT: Dadan Hindayanas, the former Head of the National Nutrition Agency (BGN), has been dismissed from his position after serving for approximately one and a half years. The decision was made by the President following a performance review, which highlighted various controversies during Dadan\'s tenure. These include his statement that drinking two liters of milk per day is beneficial for growth, as well as proposing insects and sago worms as alternative protein sources in the Free Nutritious Meal (MBG) program. Additionally, under Dadan\'s leadership, the MBG program has been linked to 446 poisoning cases with a total of 37,693 victims as of early May 2026. The procurement practices at BGN have also been criticized for being wasteful and suspicious, with examples including the purchase of 20,000 motorcycle units and shoe polish.\n\n\n',)
