2026-06-05 02:49:13 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\nYou are given a list of RawRecord objects. Each RawRecord contains:\n- raw_id\n- text\n- metadata (including a \'created\' field representing when the record was published)\n\nYour task is to infer the single canonical semantic triple that best represents\nthe shared meaning across ALL records in the list.\n\nA triple has the form:\n(subject, predicate, object)\n\nRules:\n1. The triple must express the core relation that all records instantiate.\n2. The triple must be abstract enough to cover all records, but specific enough\n   to distinguish this subgraph from unrelated content.\n3. Use canonicalized forms of entities and relations.\n4. The predicate should be a relation phrase, not a full sentence.\n5. Ignore surface details and stylistic differences.\n6. Do NOT summarize the documents. Extract the underlying relation.\n7. If multiple triples are possible, choose the one that is maximally general\n   while still being true for all records.\n\nYou must also infer contextual metadata with the following keys:\n- location\n- subject_matter\n- industry\n- time  ← IMPORTANT: this should reflect WHEN THE EVENT OCCURRED,\n         not when the records were published.\n\nYou may use the \'created\' timestamps to help disambiguate event time,\nbut you must NOT output the \'created\' timestamps themselves.\n\nOnly include a metadata field if it is stable across ALL records.\nIf a field is not stable, set it to null.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4156503\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 33771631-html\nTEXT: Diplomacy may be struggling to survive as tensions rise between Iran, Hezbollah, and the US. Sanctions relief remains tied to Iran\'s nuclear program, according to Senator Rubio, who insists that key shipping routes will not be reopened. Meanwhile, Iran-linked actors continue to test the limits of the uneasy truce, with Hezbollah rejecting a "partial cease-fire" proposal. US military officials report new Iranian missile activity against regional targets, highlighting the challenges in achieving a deal. Analyst Dania Arayssi notes that Iran often brings Lebanon into negotiations with the US, but today\'s meetings were productive and positive, with both parties agreeing on a shared objective. The Lebanese government is seeking to reclaim its sovereignty and control over its borders, while Hezbollah follows orders from Tehran. The continuation of launching missiles and strikes on Israel often coincides with slowdowns or setbacks in negotiations between Iran and the US.\n\nID: 4155826\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: turkiye-seven-countries-condemn-al-aqsa-raids-222807\nTEXT: Turkish ministers have condemned Israel\'s ongoing measures aimed at altering the historical, legal and demographic character of occupied East Jerusalem. The ministers reiterated their rejection of attempts to change the status of Jerusalem\'s Muslim and Christian holy sites, recognizing the historic Hashemite custodianship. They reaffirmed that Al-Aqsa Mosque\'s 144-dunum area is exclusively for Muslims, and the Jerusalem Awqaf department is the sole authority responsible for administering the mosque. The ministers held Israeli authorities responsible for escalatory actions, warning that repeated violations fuel instability and undermine international peace efforts. They called for an immediate end to such practices and full respect for the status quo at Al-Aqsa Mosque.\n\nID: 4155615\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: iran-condemns-us-strike-on-qeshm-island-vows-self-defense\nTEXT: Iran has strongly condemned US strikes on an Iranian oil tanker in the Strait of Hormuz and a communications tower on Qeshm Island, reaffirming its right to self-defense. The Iranian Foreign Ministry stated that the attacks violated the April 8 ceasefire agreement and constituted a breach of international law, including Article 2(4) of the UN Charter. Kuwait and Bahrain are accused of allowing the US to launch military operations against Iran from their territory, bearing "direct and clear responsibility" for the incident. The ministry also reaffirmed Iran\'s right to defend its sovereignty and territorial integrity using all available means, citing UN General Assembly Resolution 3314 as an act of aggression against Iran.\n\nID: 4156269\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: cargo-ship-explodes-off-iraq-in-latest-mideast-maritime-attack-amid-iran-war\nTEXT: A cargo ship exploded off Iraq on Monday afternoon, according to the British military. The attack occurred near Umm Qasr, Iraq, and caused a "large explosion". No one claimed the attack. This incident comes amid rising tensions in Lebanon, where Iran wants any agreement to include the country. The US military has carried out strikes in Iran on Saturday and Sunday, targeting air defenses and attack drones. The attacks have led to a significant decrease in traffic through the Strait of Hormuz, with only 36 ships transiting the waterway in the seven days leading up to Friday. The US and Israel launched the war with strikes on Iran on February 28, with Trump offering shifting goals for the conflict.\n\nID: 4156520\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: slopification-political-art-press-any-key-to-continue\nTEXT: The US threat to destroy Iranian cultural sites could lead to criminal liability under international law, specifically The Hague Convention for the Protection of Cultural Property in the Event of Armed Conflict. This convention prohibits any act of hostility to cultural property, and as a signatory, the US would be held accountable. Artist Shirin Neshat\'s exhibition at the Broad museum in LA features new work addressing discrimination in Trump\'s America, highlighting the power of political satire. The Victoria and Albert Museum\'s director, Tristram Hunt, has called on the international community to condemn President Trump\'s threat, emphasizing that cultural warfare cannot be normalized.\n\nID: 4156535\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: rubio-faces-lawmakers-as-iran-ceasefire-hangs-in-the-balance\nTEXT: US Secretary of State Marco Rubio informed lawmakers that Iran continues to possess a robust drone arsenal, with the Islamic Republic\'s Shahed-136 drones costing between $20,000 and $50,000 apiece. Despite a 38-day US bombing campaign, Iran\'s drone capabilities remain intact due to the low cost and high replaceability of the technology. Rubio stated that the US had been "highly successful" in achieving its military objectives, degrading Iran\'s Navy and industrial base. However, a ceasefire between the US and Iran remains tenuous, with recent self-defense strikes by the US and Iranian claims of targeting US forces in Kuwait.\n\nID: 4155927\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 1362666-shtml\nTEXT: Heightened tensions between Iran and the US continue to impact fragile diplomatic efforts. The ongoing talks, which have been strained since the US withdrew from the 2015 nuclear deal in 2018, saw no significant breakthroughs on Tuesday. The US and Iran have been negotiating since February 2023, with the aim of reviving the Joint Comprehensive Plan of Action (JCPOA). Despite efforts by US Secretary of State Antony Blinken and Iranian Foreign Minister Hossein Amir-Abdollahian to ease tensions, the talks remain fragile due to ongoing disagreements over nuclear issues and US sanctions.\n\nID: 4155940\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 014000c\nTEXT: UN chief Antonio Guterres proposes three options to end the Israel-Hezbollah conflict after peacekeepers leave Lebanon. The options include continuing U.N. military monitoring of the boundary between Israel and Lebanon, supporting Lebanese forces in deploying throughout the country, and strengthening political efforts to end the fighting. Guterres emphasizes the importance of implementing a 2006 resolution that demands Hezbollah disarm, Israeli forces withdraw, and the Lebanese army deploy throughout the country. The proposed options range from 5,525 to 1,980 personnel, including some unarmed military observers.\n\nID: 4156053\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 2191\nTEXT: Foreign Ministers from UAE, Jordan, Türkiye, Egypt, Indonesia, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, and Qatar issued a joint statement condemning the incursions by extremist Israeli settlers into Al-Aqsa Mosque, calling them "provocative and unacceptable actions" that violate international law. The Ministers hold Israeli authorities responsible for halting these escalatory actions, warning that repeated violations exacerbate tensions and undermine international efforts to achieve peace. They reaffirm their support for a just, lasting, and comprehensive peace based on the two-State solution, with East Jerusalem as its capital.\n\nID: 4156087\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 2218\nTEXT: Mohammed bin Ahmed Al Yamahi, Speaker of the Arab Parliament, has condemned Iranian terrorist attacks on Kuwait and Bahrain. The attacks target civilian facilities and vital infrastructure, violating international law and humanitarian principles. Al Yamahi reaffirmed the Arab Parliament\'s solidarity with Kuwait and Bahrain, supporting their measures to safeguard national security. He praised the armed forces\' readiness in responding to the attacks, calling on the UN Security Council to take a firm stance to halt further violations and preserve regional and global peace.\n\n\n',)
