2026-06-05 03:13:20 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\nYou are given a list of RawRecord objects and a topic description.\n\nTOPIC DESCRIPTION:\n"World Cup"\n\nYour task is to provide a single canonical semantic triple that captures a\nCONCRETE, SPECIFIC detail about this topic, based on the information present\nin the records. Examples include named actors taking actions, concrete events,\ndecisions, agreements, deployments, discoveries, or other factual relations.\n\nA triple has the form:\n(subject, predicate, object)\n\nGuidelines:\n- PRIORITIZE DETAIL: extract a specific, factual, topic-relevant relation.\n- AVOID GENERIC TRIPLES: do not produce vague relations like "X engages in Y".\n- CANONICALIZE: normalize entity and relation phrasing.\n- FOCUS ON THE TOPIC: the triple must illuminate a concrete aspect of the topic,\n  not a general summary.\n\nMetadata:\nInfer the following metadata fields ONLY if they are stable across the records:\n- location\n- subject_matter\n- industry\n- time  ← reflects WHEN THE EVENT OCCURRED, not publication time.\n\nYou may use \'created\' timestamps to disambiguate event time, but do NOT output them.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4155597\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: world-cup-2026-group-a-profile-four-nations-of-equal-strength\nTEXT: South Africa and South Korea are set to face off in Group A of the 2026 World Cup, with both teams boasting strong squads. South Africa, led by coach Hugo Broos, features a mix of local players and imports from Europe and the US. Goalkeepers Ronwen Williams and Ricardo Goss are expected to play key roles, while defenders Khuliso Mudau and Olwethu Makhanya provide a solid foundation. Midfielders Teboho Mokoena and Jayden Adams offer creativity, while forwards Oswin Appollis and Lyle Foster have the potential to cause problems for opposing teams.\n\nSouth Korea, meanwhile, is looking to build on their undefeated AFC qualifying campaign. The team\'s strength lies in its European-based players, including Kim Minjae and Jens Castrop. Goalkeepers Jo Hyeonwoo and Kim Seunggyu are expected to be solid in goal, while defenders Kim Minjae and Lee Hanbeom provide a strong defensive presence. Midfielders Yang Hyunjun and Paik Seungho offer creativity, while forwards Son Heungmin and Oh Hyeongyu have the potential to cause problems for opposing teams.\n\nThe two teams will meet on June 18, 2026, in a highly anticipated match.\n\nID: 4155684\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: 2026-fifa-world-cup-schedule-important-dates-and-match-stages\nTEXT: The 2026 FIFA World Cup schedule has been released, with key dates including the Round of 32 (June 28- July 3), Round of 16 (July 4-7), Quarterfinals (July 9-11), Semifinals (July 14-15) at AT&T Stadium in Arlington, Texas and Mercedes-Benz Stadium in Atlanta. The Third-place game will take place on July 18 at Hard Rock Stadium in Miami Gardens, and the Final match is scheduled for July 19 at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, New Jersey.\n\nID: 4155827\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: turkiyes-national-team-arrives-in-us-for-fifa-world-cup-222828\nTEXT: Türkiye\'s national team has arrived in the US for the FIFA World Cup, shifting focus from its friendly against Venezuela. The team will face Australia on June 13, Paraguay on June 20, and host nation U.S. on June 26 in Group D play. Based in Mesa, Arizona, the team will utilize a facility with 24 multipurpose training grounds. Captain Hakan Calhanoglu, Real Madrid midfielder Arda Guler, and Juventus forward Kenan Yildiz are expected to lead the team.\n\nID: 4156579\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: national-team-begins-world-cup-preparations-in-chicago\nTEXT: Germany\'s 26-player World Cup squad, led by coach Julian Nagelsmann, arrived in Chicago on Tuesday evening and checked into the Waldorf Astoria hotel. The team will begin preparations for the tournament immediately, with their first training session scheduled for Wednesday. They will face a pre-World Cup warm-up match against co-host USA on Saturday. The 2026 World Cup will be played in the USA, Canada and Mexico, with Germany hoping to win the championship.\n\nID: 4156217\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: final-preparations-for-french-world-cup-team-before-heading-to-us\nTEXT: France\'s World Cup team is making final preparations before heading to the US, where they will face Argentina in a rematch of their 2022 final loss. The team, led by Kylian Mbappé, will look to redeem their defeat in the 2022 final, where they were beaten in a penalty shoot-out. This will be their first World Cup appearance since 2018, when they won the title under the same team.\n\nID: 4156580\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: arrival-in-america-dfb-team-lands-in-chicago\nTEXT: The DFB team, led by coach Hans-Dieter Flick, has arrived in Chicago to begin training in the USA. They will face a friendly match against the World Cup co-hosts, the United States, on Saturday.\n\n\n',)
