ns and wounding 131 others. The attack stretched past dawn, with explosions reverberating across cities. In Dnipro, 12 people were killed and six in Kyiv. Residents have been on edge for days after Russia warned of a massive aerial attack, with no embassies reporting damage. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy appealed for more US and European support, describing the attack as "an explicit statement by Russia: If Ukraine is not protected from ballistic missiles and other missile strikes, those strikes will continue."\n\nID: 4155604\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: russia-launches-major-attack-on-ukraine-several-killed\nTEXT: Russia has launched a major attack on Ukraine, with several killed. President Zelenskyy warned of a massive strike, stating they have prepared one. Russia had previously threatened "systematic strikes" on Ukrainian military targets and decision centers in Kyiv, prompting foreigners to leave the capital. The attack comes after a drone strike on a dormitory in Russian-held Luhansk region, which killed 21 people.\n\n\n',)
