 fails to return his passport by June 24. Masuda is suspected of proposing the robbery to Kaito Takemae, an acquaintance and on-site supervisor, with a 40% reward for the ¥100 million proceeds. The six suspects, including Masuda, were arrested after a highly anonymous app was used to plan the crime. Three days after the incident, Masuda left for China from Narita International Airport and is believed to have arrived in a Southeast Asian nation.\n\nID: 4156035\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: yakuza-member-among-three-more-arrested-over-us26-mil-theft-on-tokyo-street\nTEXT: A senior Yakuza member, along with two others, have been arrested for allegedly stealing approximately $2.6 million in cash from a street in Tokyo\'s Ueno district in January. The suspects, who have already been indicted along with five others, are believed to have hidden about $3.6 million in cash from their homes and other locations. Investigators suspect the stolen money was intended to be used to buy gold in Hong Kong, and are exploring potential links to two similar cases: a robbery attempt at Tokyo\'s Haneda airport and a theft in Hong Kong.\n\n\n',)
