ed the Trump administration for initiatives such as exempting Social Security from taxes and taking action against Russian palladium imports to boost American mining. Flint claims Democrat candidates in the race are "virtue signaling" about tariffs, saying they love tariffs when other countries were tariffing the US but pretend not to like them when the US retaliates. Flint is running on his Montana roots, "consistent conservative" principles, and listening to Montanans.\n\nID: 4156323\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: brian-miller-of-helena-wins-democratic-house-primary-in-eastern-montana\nTEXT: Brian Miller, a political newcomer, won the Democratic House primary in Eastern Montana. Despite the Montana Democratic Party\'s earlier renouncement of his efforts, Miller restarted his campaign in May and ran a congenial race with Lux. Both candidates criticized the Trump administration\'s policies, including tariffs, and pledged to support each other in the general election. Miller faces an uphill battle against well-funded opponent Downing, who was unopposed in the primary.\n\n\n',)
