-racism guidance. Mark Nowak, the victim\'s father, stated that his son\'s death should lead to safer streets and not be used to create further division. Nigel Farage, leader of Reform UK, claimed it was an example of "two-tier policing" and urged people to respond with "pure cold rage", saying "white lives matter just as much as Black lives". Hampshire Police chief constable Alexis Boon emphasized the need for answers and accountability, but warned against using it as an excuse to threaten officers.\n\nID: 4156305\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nSLUG: uk-interior-minister-condemns-violent-reaction-to-handcuffed-student-s-murder-5483324\nTEXT: UK Interior Minister condemns violent reaction to handcuffed student\'s murder. The government welcomed a review of police guidelines following the sentencing of Henry Nowak\'s Sikh killer, amid controversy over how officers treat different ethnicities.\n\n\n',)
