cle bottom requiring less pain than the last. The current 40.6% reading places Bitcoin in meaningful stress territory, but not yet at the historical maximum opportunity zone. This signals a market where ETFs and institutions have replaced weaker hands, making bottoms form with progressively lower loss thresholds. The psychological mechanism behind this signal is what gives it its forward relevance, as rising supply in loss moves markets from optimism to doubt and forced patience. A retest of the descending trendline would place the market in a region that has repeatedly marked significant accumulation windows across a decade of cycles.\n\nID: 4155849\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: bitcoinist.com\nSLUG: bitcoin-setting-major-trap\nTEXT: Bitcoin\'s ascending channel structure is becoming more dangerous as it approaches its lower boundary, with the cryptocurrency currently trading around $69,316 after falling almost 5% on the day. The structure, which has been building since February\'s low, shows a sequence of higher lows forming across March. However, the upper side of the structure has already shown weakness, with a higher high above $82,000 in early May failing to build a stronger continuation. Crypto analyst Void is leaning towards a break below the structure, which could turn higher lows into a failed pattern and lead to a dump to anywhere between $54,000 and $58,000.\n\nID: 4155855\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: bitcoinist.com\nSLUG: if-bitcoin-doesnt-hold-this-level\nTEXT: Bitcoin\'s price around the $61,000-$65,000 region could determine its next chapter. The "BTC bears crash price" on TradingView.com suggests a potential surge or accumulation at lower prices. The article questions whether Bitcoin will hold this level, implying uncertainty about its future performance.\n\n\n',)
