na Bay Sands that left a woman and her child trapped. The incident occurred on an unspecified date, prior to the charges being filed. According to authorities, the offenders are also subject to a minimum of 12 strokes of the cane as punishment. The police have warned the public to exercise caution when dealing with individuals offering currency exchange services through social media or messaging platforms, advising them to use licensed money changers instead. The three men are scheduled to return to court on June 10 as investigations continue.\n\nID: 4155626\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: ibtimes.sg\nSLUG: marina-bay-sands-robbery-shock-3-arrested-after-s50000-theft-locking-woman-child-balcony-87308\nTEXT: Three Chinese nationals, aged 29-34, were arrested after a robbery at Marina Bay Sands in Singapore. The suspects locked the victim and her child on the balcony, causing minor injuries. They had boarded a flight to Shanghai at Changi Airport and were recalled to the gate, where they were apprehended. The men could face 5-20 years in prison and 12 strokes of the cane if convicted. Authorities warned people to exercise caution when dealing with individuals offering currency exchange services through social media or messaging platforms.\n\n\n',)
