n to merge its ChatGPT app, Codex coding platform and browser into a desktop "super app" is aimed at streamlining the user experience. This move, announced in March, seeks to centralize ChatGPT\'s role in users\' computer work and sharpen its focus on engineering and business customers amidst increasing competition in enterprise AI.\n\nID: 4156075\nCREATED: 2026-06-03\nDOMAIN: emirates247.com\nSLUG: 2200\nTEXT: OpenAI\'s ChatGPT has reached 1 billion global monthly active users in May, surpassing the pace of other popular apps like Google Maps and TikTok. This milestone comes three years after launch, with Sensor Tower estimating the record-breaking growth. In contrast, Anthropic\'s Claude app saw a 5% decrease in time spent on ChatGPT after installation, with Claude itself boasting 56 million global monthly active users.\n\n\n',)
